#### AGGREGATE(9,7,...) ignores both a hidden row and an error cell

- Verify: AGGREGATE(9,7,...) ignores both a hidden row and an error cell
   - Expected: _disp(sh, "Z1") equals `9`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 14 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: AGGREGATE(9,7,...) ignores both a hidden row and an error cell")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
var sh = Sheet.new("f")
sh.set_value("A1", "1")
sh.set_value("A2", "=NA()")
sh.set_value("A3", "3")
sh.set_value("A4", "4")
sh.set_value("A5", "5")
sh.hide_row(4)
sh.set_value("Z1", "=AGGREGATE(9,7,A1:A5)")
sh = recalculate_formula_cells(sh)
# Visible, non-error cells: 1, 3, 5 -> sum 9 (row 4's "4" is hidden,
# row 2's #N/A is ignored by option 7's error-skip).
expect(_disp(sh, "Z1")).to_equal("9")
```

</details>

